WEBVTT

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:36.660
Don't let up! You've got to hold 
out until everyone's evacuated!

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.710
Right...

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.750
Joey!

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.880
Everyone's evacuated!

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:59.880
Do they actually possess a 
power that can oppose us?

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:02.930
In that case...

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.890
Heroman, let's go!

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.510
Wait, Joey.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.720
Do you have a plan?

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.380
A plan?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:36.080
If not, then we need to think one up.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.880
What are you talking about, Professor?

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.560
You can't destroy those 
spheres with normal attacks.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:45.560
Even Heroman's repeated attacks 
didn't even scratch it!

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.680
You should know that better than anyone.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.940
Well, yeah, but...

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.590
And Heroman's taken considerable damage.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.230
I'm also worried about your stamina.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.240
I'm not saying to do nothing.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.120
We'll return for now, and 
think up a new plan!

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.820
That's for the best.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.830
Okay?

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:17.760
Right...

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.730
Why those...

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.460
Hey, Will...

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.270
What?

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.320
I wonder what's gonna happen to us...

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.900
Who knows?

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:40.070
Maybe they'll put us on trial or something?

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:43.470
I wonder if we can bribe them to get away?

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.870
I seriously doubt that.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.970
Then we'll be executed?

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.030
No, we won't.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.750
If they wanted to do that, we 
wouldn't have been locked up in here.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.960
Then, what'll happen to us?

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.570
How the hell should I know?

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.350
I'm never going to give up!

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.240
I'm going home, alive!

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.850
It's no use...

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:27.340
To think this planet hid an enemy with 
this level of combat ability.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.820
However there only seems to be a single one.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:34.930
It does not surpass our own attack strength.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:39.060
So there is only one thing to do.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.760
Just give up already.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.180
There's no way we can get out that way.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.660
Damn it!

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.470
There has to be a way!

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.710
There has to be...

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.780
Nick!

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:05.610
Come!

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.510
You as well.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.800
Um... We didn't come here to rebel 
against you at all, really!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.720
Nick...

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.610
What's going to happen to us?

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.090
Anything you could tell us 
would be just great...

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.010
Nick!

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.610
What else can I do?

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.750
This is all your fault anyway, Will.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:34.680
What?

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.350
Silence!

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.840
Okay! Sorry!

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.700
I'll be quiet now!

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:36.310
Is Heroman okay?

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:37.570
I think so.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.860
I replaced the broken parts.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:43.420
But, how are <i>you</i>, Joey?

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.680
I'm fine.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:50.010
It's strange... When Heroman 
got big I felt really tired.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.460
But I'm fine now.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:56.130
Anyway, Professor, what should we do now?

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:59.190
The power's out so we can't do anything.

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.440
Worry not!

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:05.570
I thought something like this might happen, 
so I installed a personal power generator.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.310
But, Joey... Are you sure 
you're feeling okay?

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.710
Yes! Just spiffy!

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.570
I'm glad to hear it!

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.080
A bicycle?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.960
So, pedal it for me.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.820
That's good, Joey. Keep going like that.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:36.860
R-Right...

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.340
Professor, what are you planning on doing?

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:42.000
I'm going to come up with a plan.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.670
In order to do that, you can't neglect 
information gathering and analysis!

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:48.340
Well, I guess so.

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:50.780
But what are you doing, specifically?

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.290
First up is hacking and 
communications interception!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.450
<i>This is the 21st armored division reporting.</i>

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.350
<i>We are currently deployed to 
the suburbs of Center City.</i>

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:14.010
<i>We are guiding evacuees, and have 
taken a defensive position.</i>

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:16.620
<i>We have nothing else to report at this time.</i>

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:17.640
What's that?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.440
Communications have ceased 
from the seventh squad!

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.250
Secure the citizens' evacuation routes!

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.390
Prepare for battle!

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:35.710
Prepare to fire...

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:36.740
Fire!

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.770
It's no use...

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:09.780
<i>Not even a scratch!</i>

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.220
<i>Don't give up!</i>

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:12.500
<i>Keep up the attack!</i>

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.340
<i>It's coming... All hands, retreat!</i>

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.750
What's going on, Professor?

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.170
Please don't rush me.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.010
I need more information!

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:45.560
I am now at the suburbs of Center City!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.230
Just look at this scene!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:54.390
The five giant spheres that 
have been released

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:58.330
are each progressing straight ahead in one 
direction, oblivious to the military's attacks.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:04.100
The Skrugg's UFO appeared suddenly from the 
sky and began to attack Center City...

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:07.770
What could be their purpose behind this?

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.750
<i>We're going to keep a close 
watch on their movements.</i>

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.890
<i>We want everyone to see what's really happen-</i>

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.720
Verify that...

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:21.680
Excuse us, but we've received some 
new information during the report.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:25.270
<i>There are new developments at Center City.</i>

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.520
I'm reporting from on top of a 
building in front of the factory.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.290
Skrugg troops are emerging from the 
factory that the Skrugg have occupied.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.480
And in incredible numbers!

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:38.550
I repeat: Skrugg soldiers are coming down 
from the factory one after another!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.230
The Skrugg are making another move.

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:48.050
This is bad. What are they planning now?

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:49.440
Um...

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:57.050
I can't just stay here doing nothing!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.060
Joey...

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.270
You...

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:05.940
I'm going.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:09.080
We can't leave the Skrugg 
to do whatever they want!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.370
I'm coming too.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.940
I should at least be able to 
attract their attention.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:15.060
Sure!

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.610
Thanks, Psy.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:21.380
Yes, it's exactly as you said.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:26.590
I wanted to come up with a plan to deal 
with those spheres if possible, but...

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.700
A guitar?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:35.810
What's that supposed to be for, Professor?

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:38.440
You're going to stop them with rock 'n' roll?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:42.650
It's true that this is nothing but a 
guitar, but there's a secret hidden here.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.940
It's just a normal speaker, right?

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:48.200
No, no... That's not all.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:53.870
In here is the amplification device that 
was installed in that weapon of theirs.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.840
What are you saying?

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:58.230
Think back...

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:04.450
Their weapon was able to create that 
powerful an air vortex from absolutely nothing!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:09.740
Using that amplification 
device, I successfully...

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.400
...amplified sound!

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.300
That's... very impressive...

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:19.090
But what's the point to go 
through all the trouble?

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.360
A reasonable question.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.930
But there is a very good reason, you see.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.360
It is merely conjecture, yes,

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:34.690
but they may communicate among themselves 
using high-frequency sound waves.

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.640
This is also merely conjecture,

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:41.760
but their hearing may also be able to detect 
sound from a much wider range than humans.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.570
That's what I've surmised!

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:46.820
So, what does it mean?

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:52.200
If you're going up against the Skrugg, this 
guitar is more of a super powerful weapon...

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:56.080
...than missiles or cannons!

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.820
Okay? I'm going to continue 
analyzing those spheres.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.160
Be careful out there.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:08.770
I don't like this.

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:09.350
Yeah...

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:11.690
But...

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:14.680
We gotta do what we gotta do.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:16.840
Yeah.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.830
Ready, Joey?

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:56.410
We're gonna play hit and away.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:59.830
We can't go up head-to-head 
against those kind of numbers.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:02.920
Once you beat the enemy, hide 
yourself and move on.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.990
We can't let them get a bead on our location.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:08.380
That way we're sure to thin 
out their numbers.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:09.330
Got it?

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:18.150
I'll try!

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:20.710
Let's go.

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:50.650
It's him!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.320
Over here!

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.120
Cross my heart and hope...

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:13.260
Oh? That's surprising.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:16.810
The professor's invention actually worked!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:18.390
Joey!

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.890
Hostilities have broken out.

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:33.890
It seems to be that white one of interest.

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.460
Good. Dispatch reinforcements.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.600
We'll finish this right at once.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.080
Display the location.

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:41.670
About that...

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.290
What is the matter?

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.410
It seems they are using the wrecked buildings

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:49.920
and passageways we are not aware 
of to keep on the move.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:53.320
We cannot pinpoint the 
enemy's precise location.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.590
What is this?

00:15:55.920 --> 00:16:00.100
Our losses are already greater than 14.

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:03.100
Using the terrain to your 
advantage? What impudence!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:06.600
In that case, it's an eye for an eye!

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:21.560
Lina!

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:24.350
Joey!

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:29.210
What are you doing around here?

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:32.520
It's dangerous, you have to hurry and escape!

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:36.400
My brother's gone, so I...

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:41.140
Anyway, hide yourself here.

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:44.090
I'll come and pick you up 
after the battle's over.

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:45.050
No!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.230
Please, Joey...

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.070
Take me along!

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:51.940
W-Why?

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:55.630
It'll be dangerous no matter where I go.

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:59.960
So staying next to you and Heroman 
is the safest place, right?

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:01.310
But...

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:04.160
I want to search for my 
brother, no matter what!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.540
So...

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.640
Please!

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.150
You just can't.

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:14.170
You'll be in danger.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.160
If I am, then protect me, okay?

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:23.730
Huh? Where's Joey?

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.030
Hey Joey, what are you...

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:28.750
Lina?

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:30.180
Oh, you're here too, Psy?

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.720
I'm so happy!

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.430
I'm getting more confident by the second.

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.010
Now, let's go.

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:52.380
Let's go.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.800
Heroman...

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.600
Attack!

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.110
That's...

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.790
...a different kind of Skrugg than before.

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:19.000
Joey!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.950
Over here!

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.740
Don't face them all at once!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.220
Heroman!

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:48.740
What's the matter, Joey?

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.480
Oh, it's nothing.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:54.550
Good, then let's try this again!

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.050
But, how?

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.460
Lina, Psy!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:21.300
Shoot, there goes our escape route!

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:38.190
I knew it... It's different than 
the enemies from before.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.470
Heroman...

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:01.800
Attack!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.980
Joey, behind you!

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:37.220
Leave this one to me!

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:39.630
You guys bust up that one!

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.370
Right!

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.720
Heroman...

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:45.420
Blast!

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.190
It's planning on taking it?

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.410
Heroman...

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.990
Finish!

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:36.100
It actually blocked...

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.190
...Heroman's attack...

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.250
W-What the hell is this?

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:13.820
Brother?!

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.090
<b>"Can you hear this voice?"</b>

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:31.560
<b>I've been calling that, always, from deep within my heart.</b>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:45.460
<b>Would you, all alone, let another lonely one be next to you?</b>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>Because together it's not lonely, it's twoly.</b>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:56.140
<b>See, you're not alone any longer.</b>

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.990
<b>Just because there's no one next to me</b>

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:02.540
<b>doesn't mean that I'm lonely!</b>

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:07.740
<b>For someone to notice this pain</b>

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:13.270
<b>that heart must have surely cried.</b>

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.650
<b>Right now, we'll crush to bits</b>

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.350
<b>the fortress of our limitless sadness!</b>

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:24.050
<b>I'll take you with me!</b>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:27.730
<b>Got it? I'm running through at full power.</b>

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:31.470
<b>To where you're waiting, left behind</b>

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:34.640
<b>in the place of tears...</b>

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.770
<b>I believe in you, with burning passion!</b>

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:43.560
<b>Come to me!</b>

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:52.710
On the next Heroman:

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:55.650
But... we still have to fight!

00:23:55.650 --> 00:23:59.910
The identity of the assassins are Lina's 
brother Will and his best friend Nick.

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:04.420
Joey and the others retreat, able to do 
nothing against their modified bodies.

00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:06.790
Joey cannot hide his trembling,

00:24:06.790 --> 00:24:11.970
but in front of the Skrugg's unrelenting 
invasion they are forced to make a new decision.

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:16.010
Next time on Heroman Episode #6: Backlash!

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:17.650
Heroman...

00:24:17.650 --> 00:24:19.060
Attack!
